WI-famig recorded an ordering deadlock: its load-bearing open question needs
a composition prototype, and the item forbids building one before the row
cost is priced. This prices it.

At the ceiling the 11-repo cohort goes 3,166 -> 4,470 emitted rows (+1,304,
x1.41); x1.22 at 50% sufficiency, x1.11 at 25%. Reported as a curve because
sufficiency needs param_to_calls, which does not exist.

Three results matter more than the headline. Measurement 0008's relative
framing used the wrong denominator -- its 298 is the rows carrying a walk
verdict, not the 3,166 the cohort emits -- so the ratio was overstated ~2.5x.
The cost is not one row per confirmation: 1,549 composable findings yield
+1,304 rows because a group whose members are all composable vanishes, and
touched groups run 1 to 104 members. And §4a would invalidate a premise the
collapse design states quantitatively -- the ddg bypass is justified because
ddg is 1.7% of flows, which reproduces today at 1.43% and would go to 13.17%.

0008's ceiling has also drifted 18.3% -> 14.8% in six days; five repos are
byte-identical and jaeger's halved. The simulation is checked against the
production collapse function on four repos and is exact on each.

